<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vache II of Albania</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">5th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vache II was a king of Caucasian Albania of the Arsacid line in the mid-fifth century. Forced by the Sasanian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yazdegerd-ii">Yazdegerd II</a> to adopt <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zoroastrianism">Zoroastrianism</a>, he returned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> and rose against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> around 459. After his defeat he abdicated, and the Albanian kingship lapsed for about a quarter of a century until its restoration under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vachagan-iii">Vachagan III</a>.</p></div>
